# React Rules

## Component Structure
- Use functional components with hooks
- Use PascalCase for component names
- Keep components small and focused
- Extract custom hooks for reusable logic
- Use descriptive prop names

## Hooks Usage
- Use `useState` for local component state
- Use `useEffect` for side effects
- Use `useCallback` for event handlers
- Use `useMemo` for expensive calculations
- Use `useContext` for global state
- Always cleanup effects to prevent memory leaks

## Component Examples
```typescript
// Good: Functional component with proper typing
interface PokemonCardProps {
  pokemon: Pokemon;
  onSelect?: (pokemon: Pokemon) => void;
}

export const PokemonCard: React.FC<PokemonCardProps> = ({ 
  pokemon, 
  onSelect 
}) => {
  const [isHovered, setIsHovered] = useState(false);

  const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
    onSelect?.(pokemon);
  }, [pokemon, onSelect]);

  return (
    <div 
      onMouseEnter={() => setIsHovered(true)}
      onMouseLeave={() => setIsHovered(false)}
      onClick={handleClick}
    >
      {/* Component content */}
    </div>
  );
};
```

## Performance Optimization
- Use `React.memo` for expensive components
- Use `useCallback` for event handlers passed to children
- Use `useMemo` for expensive calculations
- Avoid creating objects/functions in render

## Avoid
- Don't mutate props or state directly
- Don't forget to cleanup effects
- Don't create functions in render without useCallback
- Don't use class components unless necessary